  "title": "# Build: notifications-control-panel ## Brett said (verbatim) \"You need to have an administration p…",
  "asked": "# Build: notifications-control-panel ## Brett said (verbatim) \"You need to have an administration panel. I need to control all the notifications. I need you to build a console control panel to enable and control all possible notifications.\" Console plugin: one Notifications control panel. 1. Inventory every notification source in console, AmberX, axHub (banners, alerts, approvals/veto, UI Review, builds, merge queue, CI, health checks, account/limits, Follow Amber, AmberX push). Report the list. 2. One registry (notification types, source, channel). Every sender checks it before sending. 3. Panel: per type on/off, channel (banner, AmberX push, sound, console pop-up), priority, quiet hours, test send; master switch; per app. 4. REST + MCP + CLI so it can be set by voice. 5. Coordinate with running build ui-review-notify-audio (UI Review push to AmberX): register its notification type here, don't rebuild it. 6. Tests, README, screenshots to UI Review, PR to the merge queue. Do NOT land directly. Nothing removed. One session, lean chain. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
